From 66e20f5789ded87b48370ac213e63ca9892baced Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "HT9045 Machine (V906)" <Claude_RDBC_02@honprec.com>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 19:06:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] CARDDO: pci1203.carddo.setBit -- the PCIE-1203 card's own DO
 channel 0 / 1 (device DIO) -- EastSun 1008 '1203 page: add DO0 DO1 buttons'
 -> 'write the buttons first, I will test'.

Advantech example Device DIO: Acm_DevOpen -> FT_DevFunctionMap bit 7 -> Acm_DaqDoSetBit(device, channel, value). Probe
D:\HT9045\_review\probe_do1 on the machine: PCIE-1203-32AE (M0), map 0x1FC1 (bit 7 = 1), DO1 set 1 -> read back 1, 3 s later 0 -> 0.
EtherCAT/Pci1203Control.h / .cpp: kCmdDevDoSetBit at the enum end (after kCmdRingReset); wire name pci1203.carddo.setBit, target
  pci1203.carddo.bit<0|1>, value 0 / 1; Run_ accepts channel 0 / 1 only and needs no axis handle; Execute calls Acm_DaqDoSetBit(dev,
  channel, value) -- already on the allowlist, no new vendor call, no read-back. Same-line edits + one blank line replaced.
Not yet confirmed that the channel is the card's own DO rather than the ring's flat channel of that number (view.js notes the flat
  call reached 530 ring channels) -- EastSun tests it with the buttons.
tests: test_pci1203_pure.cpp +4 (parse, names, refusal without a bit, closed control refuses and issues nothing): 109/109; Pci1203Seam /
  MotorRoute / LinkWatch / ModuleCheck / Reopen, Idx1203GaliBranch, IndexZTorque1203 / AutoHeight1203, I115B_Vacuum, VacuumVc8 passed.
  Debug and release linked. Web part: web commit (same tag).
WORKLOG row 211.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
